  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/l01wWOs9K8Oebu8nCRXy0ID5sTT3DsHDSR3CxRi0xoo.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>Equation of normal to parabola<br/>$y^2=8 x \\text { is } y=m x-4 m-2 m^3$<br/>passes through $(0,-6)$ we get<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& -6=-4 \\mathrm{~m}-2 \\mathrm{~m}^3 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{~m}^3+2 \\mathrm{~m}-3=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow(\\mathrm{~m}-1)\\left(\\mathrm{m}^2+\\mathrm{m}+3\\right)=0 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{~m}=-1 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{P}=\\left(\\mathrm{am}^2,-2 \\mathrm{am}\\right)=(2,-4) \\\\\n& \\therefore \\text { Shortest distance }=\\mathrm{PC}-\\mathrm{r} \\\\\n& =(2 \\sqrt{2}-1)<br/>\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
